## Architecture

The project is a thin app shell over the `{{APP_NAME}}Kit` Swift package:

| Target | Responsibility | Depends on |
|---|---|---|
| **{{APP_NAME}}Core** | Pure-Swift domain logic. Value types, `Sendable`, `Codable`. | — |
| **{{APP_NAME}}Data** | Persistence, content, sync. No SwiftUI. | Core |
| **{{APP_NAME}}Intents** | App Intents — the app's API for Siri/Shortcuts/Spotlight. | Core, Data |
| **{{APP_NAME}}UI** | SwiftUI presentation. The app target is a thin shell over this. | Core, Data |

## Project structure

```
{{APP_NAME}}/
├── Package.swift            # {{APP_NAME}}Kit — the library targets above
├── {{APP_NAME}}/            # Xcode project: app shell + extension targets
├── Sources/                 # package sources (one folder per target)
├── Tests/                   # Swift Testing suites
├── Tools/                   # lint.sh, check-docs.sh, check-size.sh, check-project.sh, tag-release.sh
├── ci_scripts/              # Xcode Cloud hooks (tests + lint gate, version stamping)
├── ci/                      # Xcode Cloud workflow payloads (CI, TestFlight)
└── docs/                    # decision records, release process, playbooks
```

## Development

```sh
swift test              # package suites (what CI gates on)
Tools/lint.sh           # SwiftLint + SwiftFormat, same checks as CI
Tools/check-docs.sh     # public API docs
Tools/check-size.sh     # binary-size budget
Tools/check-project.sh  # project-configuration doctor
```

App and extension targets build in Xcode (scheme **{{APP_NAME}}**).

## Releasing

`Tools/tag-release.sh MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` from main — the `v*` tag triggers the TestFlight
workflow, which stamps the version and uploads all platforms. See `docs/release-process.md`.
